repository modifies or re-licenses one. Read the licence shown on each download page and keep the licence file that
comes with the weights.

DDTree — the draft tree the block drafters' trees run (XEN_DRAFTER_TREE and friends).
The tree walk is Xenithium's own implementation; the name and the idea are the authors': Liran Ringel and Yaniv
Romano, "Accelerating Speculative Decoding with Block Diffusion Draft Trees" (arXiv:2604.12989), reference
implementation https://github.com/liranringel/ddtree (MIT licensed). No code from that repository is distributed
with Xenithium; should any ever be incorporated, this file must additionally carry its copyright notice and
license text as the MIT license requires.
